Trans:
🔴 Tenth day of resistance against the aggressor. Report from the General Staff as of 6 p.m.

-The invaders have not achieved their goals, so they continue to launch missile and bomb strikes on civilian infrastructure, including using bomber aircraft;

-An air strike on Bila Tserkva damaged over 20 residential buildings;

-Bombing in Irpen damaged the railway track and disrupted a train used to evacuate civilians;

-On the approaches to Brovary, near the Victory area, the Ukrainian Armed Forces conducted an air strike on 15 separate motorized infantry brigades of the Russian Central Military District; there were losses, which are still being confirmed;

-Units of the 247th Guards Assault Regiment of the Russian Federation's Southern Military District, Colonel Konstantin Zizevsky, were killed by Ukrainian Armed Forces units.

Two planes of the Russian occupiers were shot down, three pilots were captured, and one plane was destroyed.

-Five helicopters and one enemy UAV were shot down.

-The aggressor is intensifying efforts to recruit mercenaries through so-called private military companies (PMCs), with Wagner's headquarters now located in Rostov-on-Don.

